attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a single spine column.** Column 0, `otsB`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1}. The model names 99.8% of them, at 0.11 bits {S1, M}.

@variable **The first fork is at `otsA`**, column 1, carried by 89% {S2.c1}. Then the `flhD` to `motB` genes, columns 3 to 6, [[flagellar motor]], and the `cheA` to `tap` genes, columns 7 to 10, [[chemotaxis methyl-accepting]] {S2.c3-10, Q}. A branch of 23 persistent families runs through columns 1 to 23 in 11%, [[arabinose transport and ferritin]] {S2.b1, X}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine column than on the fork and variable ones**, 99.8% against 93%, and hesitates less there, 0.11 against 0.34 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 34, `yebB`, is a variable column, at 0.73 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on a fork column.** Column 79, `manZ`, is carried by 59% of chromosomes, with `manY` at 31% and `manX` at 15% {S2.c79, E}. The last column is `manZ` {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 93% of genes**, 0.34 bits on average, perplexity 1.5 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 2.27 against 0.17 bits, and names fewer genes, 49% against 97% {C}.

